# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Important notes {#important-notes}"
msgstr "Mahahalagang tala {#important-notes}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**1. Each number is a sum over the error terms sharing a support.** Without a filter, the bounds of\n"
"every error term acting on the same qubit, or on the same pair of qubits, are added into one value:\n"
"all three Pauli types on a qubit, and all nine on a pair. That has two consequences. A value can\n"
"exceed 2.0, even though no single term's bound can (a box labelled `4.5` is several terms adding up,\n"
"not a violated bound). The figure cannot tell you whether a large value comes from one Pauli\n"
"type or from several comparable ones; the next section shows how to separate them.\n"
msgstr ""
"**1. Ang bawat numero ay kabuuan ng mga error term na may iisang support.** Kapag walang filter, ang mga bound ng\n"
"bawat error term na kumikilos sa iisang qubit, o sa iisang pares ng mga qubit, ay idinaragdag sa isang halaga:\n"
"lahat ng tatlong uri ng Pauli sa isang qubit, at lahat ng siyam sa isang pares. May dalawang kahihinatnan ito. Ang isang halaga ay maaaring\n"
"lumampas sa 2.0, kahit walang bound ng iisang term na makakagawa nito (ang box na may label na `4.5` ay ilang term na nagsasama,\n"
"hindi nilabag na bound). Hindi masasabi ng figure kung ang malaking halaga ay mula sa isang uri\n"
"ng Pauli o mula sa ilang magkakatulad; ipinapakita ng susunod na seksyon kung paano paghiwalayin ang mga ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**2. The color scale starts at 2.0 and grows with the data.** The scale runs from 0 to the\n"
"`\"max_bound\"` entry of the overlaid circuit's metadata, which is the larger of 2.0 and the largest\n"
"value shown. Unfiltered sums often exceed 2.0, so the scale stretches to fit them, and the same\n"
"color can stand for different values in different figures. When every value is small, the\n"
"scale stays at 2.0 and everything looks uniformly dark (that is the scale reflecting the absolute\n"
"size, not a rendering fault).\n"
msgstr ""
"**2. Nagsisimula ang color scale sa 2.0 at lumalaki ayon sa data.** Tumatakbo ang scale mula 0 hanggang sa\n"
"entry na `\"max_bound\"` ng metadata ng na-overlay na circuit, na siyang mas malaki sa 2.0 at sa pinakamalaking\n"
"halagang ipinapakita. Ang mga unfiltered na kabuuan ay madalas lumampas sa 2.0, kaya ini-stretch ang scale para magkasya ang mga ito, at ang parehong\n"
"kulay ay maaaring kumatawan sa magkakaibang halaga sa magkakaibang figure. Kapag maliit ang bawat halaga, nananatili ang\n"
"scale sa 2.0 at lahat ay mukhang pare-parehong madilim (iyon ay ang scale na sumasalamin sa absolute na\n"
"laki, hindi pagkakamali sa rendering).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Separating the Pauli types {#separating-the-pauli-types}"
msgstr "Paghihiwalay ng mga uri ng Pauli {#separating-the-pauli-types}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use `pauli_filter` to see one type at a time. An integer selects a Pauli weight; a string selects\n"
"a specific Pauli, matched against each noise term **reduced to its own non-identity support**. So\n"
"`\"X\"` selects every single-qubit $X$ error, regardless of which qubit it acts on, and `\"XX\"` selects the\n"
"weight-2 ones (a full-width label like `\"XII\"` matches nothing).\n"
msgstr ""
"Gamitin ang `pauli_filter` para makita ang isang uri sa bawat pagkakataon. Ang integer ay pumipili ng Pauli weight; ang string ay pumipili ng\n"
"isang tiyak na Pauli, na itinutugma sa bawat noise term na **binawasan sa sarili nitong non-identity support**. Kaya\n"
"ang `\"X\"` ay pumipili ng bawat single-qubit na $X$ error, kahit aling qubit ang kinikilusan nito, at ang `\"XX\"` ay pumipili sa\n"
"mga weight-2 (ang full-width na label gaya ng `\"XII\"` ay walang tinutugma).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The unfiltered row is the sum of the three Pauli types below it. Filtering is the only way to tell\n"
"whether a large unfiltered value comes from one dominant error type or from several comparable ones.\n"
"That matters, because the mitigation acts per term, not per site.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang unfiltered na hilera ay kabuuan ng tatlong uri ng Pauli sa ilalim nito. Ang pag-filter ang tanging paraan para malaman\n"
"kung ang malaking unfiltered na halaga ay mula sa isang nangingibabaw na uri ng error o mula sa ilang magkakatulad.\n"
"Mahalaga iyon, dahil ang mitigation ay kumikilos kada term, hindi kada site.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Passing the same filter to `draw_shaded_lightcone` records it in the figure title, so a filtered\n"
"figure cannot be mistaken for an unfiltered one:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pagpasa ng parehong filter sa `draw_shaded_lightcone` ay nagtatala nito sa pamagat ng figure, kaya ang naka-filter\n"
"na figure ay hindi mapagkakamalang unfiltered:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/interpreting-visualizations/extracted-outputs/cell-09-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/interpreting-visualizations/extracted-outputs/cell-09-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This figure looks quite different from the unfiltered one above, and not only because it shows\n"
"fewer values. Each placeholder in these figures stands for one support: a single qubit, or a pair of\n"
"qubits. Without a filter, a box shows a placeholder on every qubit and on every pair of neighboring\n"
"qubits, so it spreads over several columns. With `\"X\"`, only the single-qubit supports remain, and\n"
"each box shrinks to a single column.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ibang-iba ang hitsura ng figure na ito sa unfiltered sa itaas, at hindi lang dahil mas kaunti ang ipinapakita nitong\n"
"halaga. Bawat placeholder sa mga figure na ito ay kumakatawan sa isang support: isang qubit, o isang pares ng\n"
"mga qubit. Kapag walang filter, ang isang box ay nagpapakita ng placeholder sa bawat qubit at sa bawat pares ng magkatabing\n"
"mga qubit, kaya kumakalat ito sa ilang column. Sa `\"X\"`, ang mga single-qubit na support na lang ang natitira, at\n"
"ang bawat box ay lumiliit sa isang column.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Neither picture shows what PEC actually applies though. The placeholders are a way to display\n"
"bounds, not anti-noise gates. During the experiment, every box whose error terms are mitigated is\n"
"treated as a single layer of two-qubit gates, and the anti-noise Paulis sampled for its error terms\n"
"are composed into one Pauli that is applied to that layer as a whole.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pero wala sa alinmang larawan ang aktwal na inilalapat ng PEC. Ang mga placeholder ay paraan lang para ipakita ang\n"
"mga bound, hindi mga anti-noise gate. Sa panahon ng eksperimento, ang bawat box na may mga error term na minimitigate ay\n"
"tinatrato bilang isang layer ng two-qubit gate, at ang mga anti-noise Pauli na na-sample para sa mga error term nito\n"
"ay pinagsasama-sama sa isang Pauli na inilalapat sa buong layer na iyon.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "`animate_shaded_lightcone` {#animate_shaded_lightcone}"
msgstr "`animate_shaded_lightcone` {#animate_shaded_lightcone}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On a device whose connectivity is not a 1D line, a circuit diagram no longer shows which qubits are\n"
"neighbors, so the spatial spread of the lightcone becomes impossible to read.\n"
"`animate_shaded_lightcone` instead draws the QPU's coupling map and animates the bounds across it,\n"
"one noisy box per frame.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa isang device na ang connectivity ay hindi 1D na linya, hindi na ipinapakita ng circuit diagram kung aling mga qubit ang\n"
"magkatabi, kaya imposibleng mabasa ang spatial na pagkalat ng lightcone.\n"
"Ang `animate_shaded_lightcone` ay iginuguhit na lang ang coupling map ng QPU at ina-animate ang mga bound dito,\n"
"isang noisy box kada frame.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It needs a `CouplingMap`, which it lays out on a grid by embedding the device graph, so it handles both\n"
"heavy-hex and square connectivity.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kailangan nito ng `CouplingMap`, na inilalatag nito sa isang grid sa pamamagitan ng pag-embed ng graph ng device, kaya kaya nitong hawakan ang parehong\n"
"heavy-hex at square na connectivity.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<div class=\"alert alert-info\">\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Note:** In this rendered documentation the animation is static. The slider and play button only\n"
"work when the notebook runs interactively, for example in Jupyter.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Tandaan:** Sa na-render na dokumentasyong ito, static ang animation. Gumagana lang ang slider at play button\n"
"kapag interactive na tumatakbo ang notebook, halimbawa sa Jupyter.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
