# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reading the animation {#reading-the-animation}"
msgstr "Pagbasa sa animation {#reading-the-animation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Each qubit is a pie chart, one slice per Pauli type.** A qubit's marker is divided into three\n"
"slices for its $X$, $Y$ and $Z$ errors, each shaded by its own bound. This is the filtering from the\n"
"previous section built into the figure (no `pauli_filter` needed to tell the types apart).\n"
msgstr ""
"**Ang bawat qubit ay isang pie chart, isang slice para sa bawat uri ng Pauli.** Ang marker ng isang qubit ay hinahati sa tatlong\n"
"slice para sa mga error nitong $X$, $Y$ at $Z$, na bawat isa ay may sariling shade ayon sa bound nito. Ito ang pag-filter mula sa\n"
"nakaraang seksyon na nakapaloob na sa figure (hindi na kailangan ng `pauli_filter` para paghiwalayin ang mga uri).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Edges carry the two-qubit error bounds.** The line between two coupled qubits is shaded by the\n"
"bound on weight-2 errors acting on that pair.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Dala ng mga edge ang mga two-qubit error bound.** Ang linya sa pagitan ng dalawang magkakabit na qubit ay may shade ayon sa\n"
"bound sa mga weight-2 error na tumatama sa pares na iyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Light gray means no data, not a small bound.** A slice or an edge is drawn light gray when the\n"
"box's noise model has no error term for it, for instance on qubits the box does not act on. It is\n"
"drawn gray rather than dark so it cannot be confused with a bound of zero. Boxes beyond a\n"
"`max_num_boxes` limit are different: they carry the trivial bound of 2.0, so they are drawn at the\n"
"bright end of the scale.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Ang light gray ay nangangahulugang walang data, hindi maliit na bound.** Ang isang slice o edge ay iginuguhit na light gray kapag\n"
"walang error term para dito ang noise model ng box, halimbawa sa mga qubit na hindi ginagalaw ng box. Iginuguhit itong\n"
"gray sa halip na madilim para hindi ito mapagkamalang bound na zero. Iba ang mga box na lampas sa limitasyong\n"
"`max_num_boxes`: dala nila ang trivial na bound na 2.0, kaya iginuguhit sila sa\n"
"maliwanag na dulo ng scale.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The slider steps through boxes, not through time uniformly.** There is one frame per noisy box, in\n"
"circuit order (or in reverse order with `reverse=True`, which traces the lightcone backwards from\n"
"the observable). Watching it in reverse is usually the more intuitive direction: the cone grows\n"
"outwards from the measured qubits. Each frame is labelled with its box's identifier, the same key\n"
"under which the bounds dictionary stores that box, so the slider can also be used to jump to a\n"
"particular box and look up its numbers.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Hakbang-hakbang ang slider sa mga box, hindi pantay na sa oras.** May isang frame kada noisy box, ayon sa\n"
"ayos ng circuit (o pabaliktad gamit ang `reverse=True`, na sinusundan ang lightcone pabalik mula sa\n"
"observable). Kadalasang mas madaling maunawaan ang panonood nito nang pabaliktad: lumalaki ang cone\n"
"paitaas mula sa mga qubit na sinukat. Ang bawat frame ay may label na identifier ng box nito, ang parehong key\n"
"kung saan itinatago ng bounds dictionary ang box na iyon, kaya magagamit din ang slider para tumalon sa\n"
"isang partikular na box at hanapin ang mga numero nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Note:** The qubit layout is recovered from the coupling map's graph by embedding it into a square\n"
"lattice. A coupling map that does not embed (because it is disconnected, or too densely connected\n"
"for a grid) raises a `ValueError` rather than drawing a misleading picture.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Tandaan:** Ang layout ng mga qubit ay nakukuha mula sa graph ng coupling map sa pamamagitan ng pag-embed nito sa isang square\n"
"lattice. Ang coupling map na hindi ma-embed (dahil disconnected ito, o masyadong siksik ang koneksyon\n"
"para sa isang grid) ay magtataas ng `ValueError` sa halip na gumuhit ng nakaliligaw na larawan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Which to use {#which-to-use}"
msgstr "Alin ang gagamitin {#which-to-use}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | `draw_shaded_lightcone` | `animate_shaded_lightcone` |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| geometry | the circuit diagram | the QPU coupling map |\n"
"| best for | 1D chains | any connectivity |\n"
"| Pauli types | summed, unless filtered | always split, as pie slices |\n"
"| time | all layers at once | one layer per frame |\n"
"| output | a `matplotlib` figure | a `plotly` figure |\n"
msgstr ""
"| | `draw_shaded_lightcone` | `animate_shaded_lightcone` |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| geometry | ang circuit diagram | ang coupling map ng QPU |\n"
"| pinakamainam para sa | mga 1D chain | anumang connectivity |\n"
"| Mga uri ng Pauli | pinagsama, maliban kung na-filter | laging hiwalay, bilang mga pie slice |\n"
"| oras | lahat ng layer nang sabay | isang layer kada frame |\n"
"| output | isang `matplotlib` figure | isang `plotly` figure |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For a 1D chain the static figure is easier to take in at a glance and reproduces in a paper. Beyond\n"
"1D the animation is the only one of the two that shows the spatial structure faithfully.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa 1D chain, mas madaling makuha sa isang sulyap ang static na figure at maaaring i-reproduce sa isang paper. Lampas sa\n"
"1D, ang animation lang sa dalawa ang nagpapakita nang tapat ng spatial na istruktura.\n"
